From dbf1cd9e60ea3f99a0f453b2018452bb53b19b50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:50:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Apply Hila's Oct 20, 2026 feedback across the patient site

- Back/Next buttons on every Learn page; repeated title lines removed
- Page descriptions moved from the banner into the page body (removed on How common)
- Figures and pictures placed before the text they illustrate
- New pictures: family, pregnancy, transplant, genetic counselors (in person, telehealth), law/ethics, 1-in-10 people
- How can genetic testing help? rebuilt as five boxes with icons and Read more links
- Hover/tap definitions for "relatives" and "DNA" on Help your family
- Hila's text edits on How common, Guide care, Help your family, Support living donor decisions,
  Signs testing may help, How testing works, Types of tests, Genetic counselors, Your rights,
  APOL1, VUS, Sharing with family, Support groups, Research opportunities and How to get tested
- New references: Elefant et al. 2025 (Types of tests), American Kidney Fund (avoid a biopsy)
- Family-sharing research (Wynn 2021) moved to the doctor resources page
- "Learn" renamed "Learn More"; path-to-testing figure on How to get tested
- Search index rebuilt for the changed pages

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FrXSTp2RFdprNw9BzY9uEe
